I had a friend in high school who was trying to get me to join 
Mensa for a while.  I had a strong anti-elitist streak then, so I 
kept dissing him about it until he left me alone.  (My PSAT scores 
would have been enough to get me in, so the test wasn't an issue.)  
Later, browsing through their main periodical (whose name I forget) 
in a laundromat, I was happy I'd never joined.  What particularly 
stands out in my mind is a pathetic story about a little boy who 
was "conducting a series of experiments on the crystalline 
structure of iodine", or something equally awful, and who kept 
writing to Santa asking for a new oscilloscope. I could almost 
smell the odor of despair rising off the pages of this magazine.

In short, I think that if you took Extropians and stripped them of 
sex appeal, a sense of humor, free-market ideas, and real-world 
achievements, you end up with something resembling Mensans. 

